# Archestimator Cursor Adapter

Cursor is an execution surface, not a separate policy source.

## Startup

<!-- supermemory-bootstrap: required -->
1. Run `bun run supermemory:ensure`.
2. Read `AGENTS.md`.
3. Read only the FAST PATH in `.ai/10_state/current-state.md`.
4. Inspect `git status --short --branch` before edits.
5. Pull only the task-relevant system, spec, design, or glob-scoped rule.

## Routing

Use Direct, Brief, or Plan Pack from `AGENTS.md`. Inherit automatic
`Q0_CONTRACT_ONLY`, `Q1_CHANGE_GATE`, `Q2_CRITICAL_CHANGE_GATE`, and
`Q3_RELEASE_GATE` classification, standing local quality authorization, and
fail-closed completion from
`.ai/00_system/BETA_QUALITY_ENGINEERING_PROTOCOL.md`.

When orchestration is selected, use
`.ai/08_prompts/000_Planning Prompts/Multi-Agent-Execution-Directive.md`.
Cursor threads use the same assignment IDs, file ownership, synchronization,
handoff, recovery, and lead-owned completion contracts. Without parallel
support, emulate passes sequentially and do not claim independent review.

Current source, `wrangler.jsonc`, local Next 16 documentation, and
`.ai/00_system` supply detail. Preserve unfamiliar work, keep one writer per
mutable file/resource, and report only evidence actually collected.
